Package: ucabled
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         acl,
         bluez,
         dbus,
         polkitd | policykit-1,
         systemd
Recommends: ucable-agent
Suggests: ucable-gnome-agent
Description: virtual FIDO2 key that relays passkeys to a phone
 ucabled registers a virtual USB HID FIDO2 device with the kernel
 (/dev/uhid) and relays WebAuthn registration and authentication
 requests from the browser to a phone over caBLE v2, the hybrid
 transport described in CTAP 2.2 section 11.5.
 .
 A QR code is shown on the desktop; the phone scans it, proves its
 proximity over Bluetooth Low Energy and completes the ceremony through
 a WebSocket tunnel, so Face ID or a fingerprint on the phone authorizes
 the request.  No key material is stored on the machine: the virtual
 device only relays the ceremony.
 .
 This package contains the system daemon, the udev rule, the D-Bus and
 polkit policies and the systemd unit.  Install ucable-agent (the default
 GTK4 session agent) or ucable-gnome-agent (a GNOME Shell extension) to
 show the prompts; the daemon cannot complete a ceremony without one.

Package: ucable-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ucabled (= ${binary:Version})
Breaks: ucabled (<< 0.2.0~)
Replaces: ucabled (<< 0.2.0~)
Description: per-user session agent for ucabled
 The ucable-agent user service runs inside each graphical session.  It
 registers with the ucabled daemon over the system bus and spawns
 ucable-agent-helper, a GTK4 window that shows the passkey QR code and
 the device-selection question.
 .
 This is the default session agent.  ucable-gnome-agent can replace it
 on GNOME; the daemon has a single agent slot, so enable only one.

Package: ucable-gnome-agent
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ucabled (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: gnome-shell
Breaks: ucabled (<< 0.2.0~)
Replaces: ucabled (<< 0.2.0~)
Description: GNOME Shell agent extension for ucabled
 This GNOME Shell extension registers with the ucabled daemon as the
 session agent and draws the passkey QR prompt and the device-selection
 question as shell modal dialogs.  It needs no helper process and no GTK
 window.
 .
 It replaces ucable-agent, the default session agent.  The daemon has a
 single agent slot, so disable ucable-agent.service when using it.  The
 extension is installed system-wide but stays disabled until each user
 runs "gnome-extensions enable ucable-gnome-agent@fuzy.me".
